---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const updated = 'October 8, 2026';
const title = `Privacy Policy | ${SITE.name}`;
const description = `How ${SITE.name} handles calculator inputs, server-assisted features, local storage, subscriptions, and advertising.`;
---

<LegalLayout title={title} description={description} heading="Privacy Policy" updated={updated}>
  <div class="legal-note">
    <p>
      <strong>The short version:</strong> Many calculators run in your browser, but some
      features send inputs to a server or save readings on your device. Subscriptions
      require contact information; analytics and advertising may use cookies after consent.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how {SITE.name} ("we", "us", or "our") handles
    information when you visit our website and use our free health calculators and
    tools (the "Service"). By using the Service, you agree to the practices described
    here.
  </p>

  <h2>2. The data you enter into our tools</h2>
  <p>
    Many calculators (such as the BMI, calorie, and body-fat tools) run entirely in
    your web browser using client-side JavaScript. The values you enter — your
    height, weight, age, activity level, and similar inputs — are processed locally
    on your device to show your result.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some features work differently. Recipe analysis sends the recipe text and servings
    through our frontend to our CMS for analysis. Downloading a share image sends the
    result parameters to our image endpoint. The HRV log and Food and Symptom Diary save
    readings and entries in your browser's local storage; Health Score saves a summary
    of your assessment there. This data remains until you clear it or your browser's
    site data. Avoid entering
    identifying or sensitive medical information into free-text fields.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Information we may collect automatically</h2>
  <p>
    Like most websites, our hosting and analytics providers may process limited
    technical information when you visit, such as:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your approximate region (derived from your IP address)</li>
    <li>Browser type, device type, and operating system</li>
    <li>The pages you view and how you arrived at the site</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider may process access logs when you visit. If you accept
    analytics, we also send page paths and performance metrics to our own endpoint;
    these records include a timestamp and approximate country and help us keep the
    site reliable. This optional measurement does not run before consent. See our
    <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>
    We use a small amount of local storage to remember your cookie-consent choice so
    we don't ask you on every visit. We send optional performance measurements and load
    third-party analytics and advertising scripts only after you accept them. To withdraw
    consent after loading them, clear this site's
    data in your browser and reload; you may also need to clear third-party cookies. Full details
    are in our <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    Hosting, analytics, and advertising providers may process technical data according
    to their own policies. If you submit an email address to subscribe or request an
    offer, we send it to our CMS and may forward it to our email automation provider
    to deliver updates. You can contact us to ask about or delete a subscription.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The Service is intended for a general adult audience and is not directed to
    children under 13 (or the equivalent minimum age in your country). We do not
    knowingly collect personal information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live (for example, under the GDPR in the UK and EU, or the
    CCPA in California), you may have rights to access, correct, or delete personal
    information, and to object to certain processing. No account is required for the tools,
    but subscriptions and server-assisted features may process information. If you have a request, please
    <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Data security</h2>
  <p>
    We serve the site over encrypted HTTPS connections and follow industry-standard
    practices to protect the limited technical data our providers process. No method
    of transmission or storage is ever completely secure, but keeping calculations on
    your device greatly reduces risk by design.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we'll revise the
    "Last updated" date above. Significant changes will be highlighted on this page.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please
    reach out through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
